VereineTaxErrorCode=The code has 2 to 32 capital letters, digits or _ and starts with a letter.
VereineTaxErrorCodeExists=A tax profile with this code exists already.
VereineTaxErrorLabel=The label is missing or longer than 255 characters.
VereineTaxErrorSphere=Choose a sphere.
VereineTaxErrorTreatment=Choose a VAT treatment.
VereineTaxErrorRate=The rate does not fit the chosen VAT treatment.
VereineTaxErrorNoteRequired=When no VAT is charged because of an exemption, the invoice must say so. Enter an invoice note, for example "VAT exempt, small business". (§ 11 (1) no. 3 lit. e UStG)
VereineTaxErrorNoteLength=The invoice note can have at most 1000 characters.
VereineTaxErrorIdealNoSupply=Nothing is sold in the idealistic sphere. Only "No VAT: nothing sold" fits.
VereineTaxErrorNonbusinessSphere="No VAT: nothing sold" only fits fees, donations, grants and interest, so the idealistic sphere or asset management. A festival or business sells something.
VereineTaxErrorHobbySphere=The tax office assumes Liebhaberei only for auxiliary businesses and festivals. Letting or a business that runs like a shop follows the normal VAT rules.
VereineTaxErrorReducedHarmful=The 10 %% for non-profit associations does not apply to a business that runs like a normal shop. (§ 10 (2) no. 4 UStG)
VereineTaxErrorSportHarmful=The VAT exemption for sports clubs covers the sports business only, not a business that runs like a normal shop. (§ 6 (1) no. 14 UStG)
VereineTaxHowToTitle=How it works
VereineTaxHowTo1=What kind of income is it? That decides the area of the association (technical term: sphere). Each area is explained below with examples.
VereineTaxHowTo2=Is VAT due? That decides the VAT treatment. The rate need not be entered, it follows from it.
VereineTaxHowTo3=What does the invoice say? When no VAT is charged, the invoice note explains why. For an exemption it is required.
VereineTaxSpheresTitle=The areas of an association
VereineTaxTreatmentsTitle=When VAT is due
VereineTaxLegalBasis=Legal basis
VereineSphereHelp_ideal=Everything the association does not sell: genuine membership fees, donations, grants, free talks or courses. Careful: when a member gets something specific for the fee, for example a course or sports equipment, it is no genuine membership fee.
VereineSphereHelp_assets=The association's assets earn money: interest from an account, letting rooms or buildings. Letting follows the normal VAT rules.
VereineSphereHelp_essential=Income directly connected with the purpose in the statutes, without which the purpose could not be reached. Examples: a theatre association's performance, admission at a museum association, lessons and admission to events at a sports club. The association may not compete with businesses more than necessary.
VereineSphereHelp_auxiliary=Income that fits the association but is not strictly needed for its purpose. Examples: carnival ball, summer festival, anniversary party, flea market.
VereineSphereHelp_festival=A festival organised essentially by members and their relatives. Outside helpers work for free, musicians or artists cost at most EUR 1,000 an hour, members provide the food. All such festivals together last at most 72 hours a year. If a condition is not met, it is a large festival and belongs to the business harmful to tax privileges.
VereineSphereHelp_harmful=Everything that runs like a normal business and fits no other area. Examples: a canteen the association runs itself, a large festival, selling goods. VAT and corporate tax are due. Up to EUR 100,000 turnover a year the association keeps its tax privileges.
VereineTreatmentHelp_nonbusiness=For income without consideration: genuine membership fees, donations, grants, interest. Nothing is sold, so there is no VAT.
VereineTreatmentHelp_hobby=For auxiliary businesses and festivals the tax office normally assumes the association makes no lasting profit (technical term: Liebhaberei). Then no VAT is charged, but the association cannot deduct input VAT either.
VereineTreatmentHelp_small_business=For associations whose taxable income is at most EUR 55,000 gross a year. Income from auxiliary businesses does not count. The invoice must say that the supply is VAT exempt.
VereineTreatmentHelp_sport=Only for associations whose statutory purpose is physical sport: their income from the sports business is VAT exempt, a canteen or festival is not. Whether e-sports counts, please clarify with the tax advisor.
VereineTreatmentHelp_reduced10=The reduced rate for non-profit associations without Liebhaberei. Not for a business harmful to tax privileges.
VereineTreatmentHelp_reduced13=For certain supplies, for example admission to sports events, theatre and music performances or museums.
VereineTreatmentHelp_standard20=The normal rate. It applies when neither an exemption nor a reduced rate fits.
